---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import NewsletterSignup from '../components/NewsletterSignup.astro';
import MyVideoAskSection from '../components/MyVideoAskSection.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Samuel Michelot: AI systems and second brains"
  description="Why Samuel Michelot built YAIBOS, how he runs several businesses without full-time employees, and how you can help build on the open specification.">
  <Header activePage="about" />

  <main class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      
      <!-- Top Profile Intro Header -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center pb-12 mb-12 border-b border-slate-200/80">
        <div class="md:col-span-8 space-y-4">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 text-xs font-mono text-blue-700">
            <span>Founder and operator</span>
          </div>

          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 font-sans leading-tight">
            Hi, I'm Samuel Michelot.
          </h1>

          <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 font-light leading-relaxed">
            I'm a software engineer, former tech founder, and systems architect based near Barcelona, Catalonia.
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-500">
            <span>• Co-founder of MosaLingua (acquired)</span>
            <span>• Founder of Simple AI Studio</span>
            <span>• Creator of the YAIBOS open spec</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="md:col-span-4 flex justify-center">
          <div class="relative">
            <div class="w-52 h-64 sm:w-60 sm:h-72 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border-2 border-slate-200 shadow-md">
              <img
                src="/images/samuel.jpg"
                alt="Samuel Michelot"
                class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top"
                loading="eager"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="absolute -bottom-3 -right-3 px-3 py-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-700 text-[11px] font-mono shadow-xs">
              Barcelona, Catalonia
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Narrative Body -->
      <div class="space-y-12 text-slate-700 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Section 1: Background -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            After MosaLingua
          </h2>
          <p>
            For over a decade, I helped build MosaLingua, a language learning platform that reached millions of learners worldwide. I worked on the software, grew the infrastructure, and managed remote teams. We bootstrapped the company and eventually sold it.
          </p>
          <p>
            After the sale, I wanted less chronic stress and more control over my time. I wanted systems that made room for life outside screens.
          </p>
          <p>
            I wanted to see how much I could run on my own with documented processes and AI agents, while keeping management overhead low.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2: How I built my AI OS -->
        <section class="space-y-4 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            How I run several businesses without full-time employees
          </h2>
          <p>
            Today, I run several projects: Simple AI Studio for business AI training and advisory, My Inner Center for wellness, and AsynCoaching for asynchronous coaching and operations.
          </p>
          <p>
            I have no full-time employees. AI agents help me qualify client leads, match invoice tables against bank statements, and test code. They also draft research newsletters each week.
          </p>
          <p>
            The setup has three parts:
          </p>
          
          <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2 text-sm font-sans">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 block mb-1">1. An open second brain</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                I keep my second brain in plain Markdown files that I own, with Obsidian as the viewer and editor. The files stay readable outside the app.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 block mb-1">2. Reusable skills</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                I document each business workflow as a procedure that people and AI agents can follow safely.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 block mb-1">3. Agents on my machine</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                Agents run on my machine, read my operating rules, and use MCP tools. I use my AI plans to avoid surprise metered API bills.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3: Second Brain & PKM Deep-Dive -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            Why I keep a second brain
          </h2>
          <p>
            Tiago Forte’s <strong>Building a Second Brain</strong> teaches how to capture and organize useful information. Nick Milo’s <strong>Linking Your Thinking</strong> focuses on developing ideas through connected notes. YAIBOS draws on both approaches for business context.
          </p>
          <p>
            I use personal knowledge management (PKM) in daily business work. Company policies, customer notes, and technical workflows live in open Markdown files, where AI assistants can read them before acting.
          </p>
          <p>
            Keeping that context in a structured second brain saves me from explaining the same business rules in every conversation. The agent can read my values, boundaries, and procedures there.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 pt-1">
            Read more about the thinkers and frameworks that shaped YAIBOS on the <a href="/inspirations" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">inspirations page</a>
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4: Simple AI Studio -->
        <section class="space-y-4 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-blue-50/40 border border-blue-100">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-blue-700 uppercase font-semibold">
            <span>Live training</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            The AI Bootcamp at Simple AI Studio
          </h2>
          <p>
            Through <a href="https://simpleaistudio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold underline">Simple AI Studio</a>, I run the AI Bootcamp to help founders, managers, and small teams set up an AI Business OS (AIBOS) they control.
          </p>
          <p>
            We build the system on participants' laptops. They organize their team's knowledge in open Markdown files, turn recurring manual work into skills, and run those skills through an existing AI harness. The files and workflows remain theirs to keep.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-slate-600 pt-2">
            Explore the bootcamp curriculum at <a href="https://simpleaistudio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-700 underline font-semibold">simpleaistudio.com ↗</a>
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5: The Invitation to Build with the Community -->
        <section class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            Why I published an open spec
          </h2>
          <p>
            Tools such as CrewAI, LangChain, and Claude Code give developers a lot to work with, but they can be hard for non-technical staff to use. Commercial SaaS products can tie company data to a vendor and add unpredictable token markup fees. I wanted a setup I could keep control of.
          </p>
          <p>
            I want small business owners to be able to launch procedures with one click, use their own AI subscriptions, and keep company knowledge in open Markdown files. The files come first; the Cockpit and Team profiles describe the extra capabilities needed for a dashboard and shared work.
          </p>
          <p class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-amber-50/50 border border-amber-200 text-slate-800 text-base font-sans">
            I published YAIBOS as an open architectural specification. I chose this over launching a closed, venture-backed SaaS because I want founders, people interested in PKM, developers, and operators to build open implementations together.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can help by building a one-click skill runner or a desktop client, improving the role permissions (RBAC) specification, or sharing how you organize your company's second brain.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 6: Connect with Samuel -->
        <section class="pt-6 border-t border-slate-200/80 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-sans">
            How to get involved
          </h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm font-mono text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-blue-600 font-bold">1.</span>
              <span>Read and star the open specification on <a href="https://github.com/orbitaloop/yaibos" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">GitHub ↗</a>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-blue-600 font-bold">2.</span>
              <span>Subscribe below for weekly notes on sovereign AI and PKM workflows.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-blue-600 font-bold">3.</span>
              <span>Send me an asynchronous voice note, video, or message via <a href="https://contact.samuelmichelot.com/?lang=en&source_site=yaibos" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">MyVideoAsk ↗</a>.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Newsletter Signup Block -->
  <NewsletterSignup variant="card" />

  <!-- Async VideoAsk Section -->
  <MyVideoAskSection />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
